>>
Rule 1 (input tensor must have at least 3 dimensions)
{v_1 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) ≥ 3
>>
Rule 2 (integer sections must be positive)
{v_2 : int} |= v_2 > 0
>>
Rule 3 (integer sections must evenly divide the depth dimension)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : int} |= ndim(v_1) ≥ 3 ∧ v_2 > 0 ∧ shape(v_1, 2) % v_2 = 0
>>
Rule 4 (list of split indices: in-range and strictly increasing)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : list(int)} |= ndim(v_1) ≥ 3 ∧ (if v_2.len ≥ 1 then ∀i ∈ [0, v_2.len - 1] : 0 ≤ v_2[i] ∧ v_2[i] ≤ shape(v_1, 2)) ∧ (if v_2.len ≥ 2 then ∀j ∈ [0, v_2.len - 2] : v_2[j] < v_2[j + 1])
>>
Rule 5 (tuple of split indices: in-range and strictly increasing)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tuple(int)} |= ndim(v_1) ≥ 3 ∧ (if v_2.len ≥ 1 then ∀i ∈ [0, v_2.len - 1] : 0 ≤ v_2[i] ∧ v_2[i] ≤ shape(v_1, 2)) ∧ (if v_2.len ≥ 2 then ∀j ∈ [0, v_2.len - 2] : v_2[j] < v_2[j + 1])
